redirects/inlinetab.html:
Create an inline tab switcher with responsive desktop/mobile variants using vanilla JavaScript.

### Structure
* Desktop: .inline-tab-wrapper { display:flex; gap:40px; border-top:1px solid #ddd; border-bottom:1px solid #ddd; padding:14px } — display:none at max-width:767px
* Each .inline-tab { color:#999; font-family:proxima-nova; font-size:12px }
* .inline-tab.active { color:#000 }
* Mobile: .mobile-tab-dropdown { display:none on desktop, display:block on mobile; border-top:1px solid #ddd; border-bottom:1px solid #ddd }
* .mobile-tab-dropdown-header { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; justify-content:center; font-weight:700 }
* SVG .arrow.rotate { transform:rotate(180deg) }
* .mobile-tab-dropdown-content: dropdown list of tabs; active item hidden via .mobile-tab-dropdown-content .inline-tab.active { display:none }

### Behaviour
* switchInlineTab(type, el) hides all .tab-panel, shows target by id, syncs .active across both desktop and mobile tabs by matching onclick string
